body:
Reduce message prompts for outdated/wrong dependency entries.  Avoid outputting error messages every time the editor is focused.

Because there are many possible causes for this situation, no automatic repair is provided.

Possible reasons include:

1. The dependency's extension is no longer valid (Loader/Importer failure);
2. Only the file was moved, its uid/import file was not moved (Incomplete file movement);
3. Its uid/import file and the filesystem cache file have been removed when the editor is launched (Accidentally removed and cannot be recovered);
4. User manually edits file.

Additionally, creating a `.gd` file with the same name using the same template in the same path will assign the same UID (unless the UID is already in use). 

Move the `.gd` file outside the editor but not its `.uid` file, focus editor, then create a file with the same name in the same location. The UID is still valid within the project, but the file content may differ with modifications. Therefore, fix dependencies as soon as the warning appears, ideally moving the file along with its uid/import files to avoid this.

